(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#" :text "Native-only overlay (plan SH unit PRELUDEASL-0): an ASL SHA-256 over Bytes, named bytesSha256 after the C builtin asl/host/src/prelude.c bSha256 it replaces on the native path (never on the VM, which keeps the C builtin since P1 measured this ASL version 6300-7900x slower interpreted). FIPS 180-4 SHA-256: pads the message (0x80, zero bytes, the 64-bit big-endian bit length) to a multiple of 64 bytes, runs the 64-round compression function over each block with the eight working variables kept as Int64 in 0..2^32-1 (never a native wrapping add or shift, since ASL Int64 traps on overflow: every + and * here is proven to stay inside int64 by the caller's own bound before the mask), and returns the eight final words as 64 lowercase hex characters, matching bSha256's own return value exactly.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/zstd.asl#" :text "Native-only Zstandard decoder overlay; interpreted asl-host keeps the faster C implementation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#" :text "R1 host prelude: the asl/prelude/prelude.asn names the C floor does not bind, written in ASL over the floor and the existing host builtins. The host loads this module before any other; a module's own definitions shadow it, and it shadows the C builtins. Failures are loud: a malformed argument traps through preludeTrap instead of yielding a default.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeHead" :text "listHead, listTail and stringSlice return Option; these unwrap where the caller has checked the bound, so a none is a prelude bug and traps (non-exhaustive match)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#resultOr" :text "moved from asl/host/src/prelude.c (plan RT-PRELUDE P3a): the (Result T E) annotation on r makes a literal non-Result argument trap ERR_TYPE_MISMATCH at load time, as optionOr's (Option T) annotation already does, in place of the host want()'s ERR_TYPE; a non-Result value that only becomes ill-typed at run time (reaches the annotation dynamically, past static checking) instead falls through mt to ERR_MATCH_NONEXHAUSTIVE, an intentional error-code change scoped to already-ill-typed programs")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeLengthFrom" :text "moved from asl/host/src/prelude.c (plan RT-PRELUDE P3b): listLength, listReverse, range, map, filter and fold as self tail calls, so a million-element list runs in constant stack; the (List T) annotation makes a non-List argument trap ERR_TYPE_MISMATCH in place of the host want()'s ERR_TYPE")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeAppendSpan" :text "LISTAPPEND-1PASS: listReverse a then preludeRevOnto onto b conses a's n elements twice (once reversing it, once un-reversing it back onto b), 2n new cons cells for an n-element a. A direct single-pass (cons x (listAppend xs b)) conses each element once but is not tail recursive, so its native stack frame depth grows with a's own length, unsafe past a few thousand elements let alone the 1e6-element lists this must still handle. preludeAppendChunks instead walks a once in O(1)-stack, allocation-free strides of preludeAppendSpan (preludeChunkStarts, tail recursive, consing nothing but one pointer per span) and conses each span onto the accumulated result in a single bounded-depth pass (preludeAppendBounded, recursion depth capped at preludeAppendSpan regardless of a's length): n elements, n new cons cells, and a native/interpreted call stack that never exceeds preludeAppendSpan frames.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeBytesEq" :text "STRFIND-NOALLOC: preludeFind and preludeSplit used to slice a fresh k-byte String at every candidate position just to compare it against t/sep with =, allocating on every position scanned rather than only at a true match; preludeBytesEq instead compares via bytesGet over Bytes the caller converts once (stringToBytes), so a scanned-and-rejected position costs no allocation at all, and only an actual matched or final piece is ever sliced back out as a String")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeRankPow5" :text "treap rank: two 31-bit lanes mod 2^31-1, each step t = h*m + byte + c then t^5 (a bijection since gcd(5, 2^31-2) = 1), so the state is 62 bits and no byte window collides independently of the state; every product stays below 2^62")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeRankNegZero" :text "a float -0.0 outside string quotes, i.e. \"0.0\" after the minus and no further digit, is ranked as 0.0 because the two compare equal")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeRankStep" :text "q is 0 outside a string literal, 1 inside, 2 after a backslash inside")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeRank" :text "the rank hashes the printed form of (list k), where string contents are quoted, so the -0.0 rule never touches a string key")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeIoError" :text "a host IO failure is the message \"KIND: PATH: reason\"; KIND names the IoError case")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeUtf8Tail" :text "charCode is the Unicode code point of the first character, decoded from its UTF-8 bytes; an empty string traps")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeLow" :text "bit operations on two's complement Int64: a value is its sign bit and its low 63 bits, a non-negative Int64 taken apart by / and mod")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeAndBits" :text "LANG-BITOPS-SYM/D143 zeroHandwrittenC: & | ^ ~ are plain ASL, not a host builtin; the old bitAnd/bitOr/bitXor took an `op` lambda (preludeBits op a b) and built one fresh closure on every call, which was the actual BITOPS-NATIVE allocation cost (the per-bit recursion itself was already small). preludeAndBits/preludeOrBits/preludeXorBits below are three plain recursive functions, each with its own combining rule inlined, so no closure is built at all; the native compiler lowers &, |, ^ and ~ to single instructions by name (NATIVE-PERF), the same way << and >> already are, and never runs this ASL body")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeB64Char" :text "base64 (RFC 4648, padded): decoding rejects characters outside the alphabet and misplaced padding")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeFnvMul" :text "FNV-1a 64 over the UTF-8 bytes: h = (h xor byte) * 1099511628211 mod 2^64, the prime being 2^40 + 435; the product is built from the 32-bit halves of h read unsigned, so no Int64 step overflows")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#listAll?" :text "ELAUDIT-C3: matches on (listTail xs) directly (as preludeDropSpan already did) instead of optionOr(listTail xs)(list), which wasted an object per element beyond the host's unavoidable Option-wrapper cost")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#listTake" :text "ELAUDIT-C3: matches on (listTail xs) directly (as preludeDropSpan already did) instead of optionOr(listTail xs)(list), which wasted an object per element beyond the host's unavoidable Option-wrapper cost")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#listDrop" :text "ELAUDIT-C3: matches on (listTail xs) directly (as preludeDropSpan already did) instead of optionOr(listTail xs)(list), which wasted an object per element beyond the host's unavoidable Option-wrapper cost")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#listAny?" :text "ELAUDIT-C3: matches on (listTail xs) directly (as preludeDropSpan already did) instead of optionOr(listTail xs)(list), which wasted an object per element beyond the host's unavoidable Option-wrapper cost")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeMathTest.asl#" :text "Gate for PRELUDEASL-A: the 22 math, conversion and time builtins (int64ToFloat64 float64ToInt64 floor ceil round clamp pow exp log log2 log10 sqrt sin cos tan atan2 abs min max nowNs monotonicNs sleepMs) reach neither prelude.c nor an abi.c ENTRY wrapper from native code. (1) The runtime declarations name none of the seven deleted asl_rt_b_ wrappers (abs min max int64ToFloat64 float64ToInt64 nowNs monotonicNs), and the IR of a program calling all 22 directly and as function values (map, fold and let-bound closures) neither declares nor calls them, nor holds a @name.<builtin> constant, which is how asl_rt_builtin is asked for a builtin by name; abs, min, max, clamp and the conversions call ssa.asl's @mathrt helpers and the clocks and sleepMs sysRoute's clock table. (2) Native stdout and exit equal asl-host run's for each case group, and a failing case's one native stderr line is the message asl-host run reports: abs, min and max on Int, Float, NaN, -0.0 and Int64 min; clamp in range, out of range, lo > hi, a NaN bound and a non-Float; float64ToInt64 at and past the int64 range, NaN and the infinities; int64ToFloat64 of 2^53+1; every libm name on edge inputs; sleepMs 0, 5 (monotonicNs advancing at least 5 ms) and -1; nowNs within 5 s of date +%s. Compiles straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker step: asl-checker rejects a builtin used as a value and has no clamp (pre-existing gaps outside this unit's :owns), as nativeOverlayTest also bypasses it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeMathTest.asl#deletedEntries" :text "The seven abi.c ENTRY wrappers this unit deletes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeMathTest.asl#compiled" :text "path straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as asl1 build does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeMathTest.asl#optBin" :text "LLVM's opt from a known homebrew location or PATH, for -passes=verify over the emitted IR; none when the host has none.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeMathTest.asl#testFailingParity" :text "asl-host run reports a failed run as FAIL <file>: CODE: message (after N asserts); the native binary writes CODE: message as its one stderr line.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#" :text "Gate for PRELUDEASL-0: a program calling bytesSha256 directly and as a value (map bytesSha256 over a list) links through asl-ir/link's opBuiltin rewrite to the native overlay's ASL definition (asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl) instead of asl_rt_builtin, its native output equals asl-host run byte for byte on the NIST vectors, the 0..130-byte padding-edge range and a 64KiB input, a 1 MiB input finishes within a generous CPU-time bound and matches asl-host run too, and each name both in lower.asl builtinArity and defined in prelude.asl at this unit's base (floatNan, floatInf, floatNegInf) gives the same native and asl-host output now that the opBuiltin rewrite reaches the real prelude as well as the overlay. Compiles straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgram, as multiModuleTest's compilePackageToLlvm! does past its checker step: asl-checker/types builtinSig has no entry for bytesSha256 (a pre-existing gap outside this unit's :owns), so the checker rejects it before a program ever reaches the linker")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#hugeFixtureSrc" :text "A standalone entry calling bytesSha256 on a 1 MiB input and printing the digest and the call's wall milliseconds (reported only; the bound is on the process's CPU time, measured by the test), kept separate from fixtureSrc so the 64KiB-and-under cases, which also run interpreted for parity, do not pay this one's cost.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#compiled" :text "entryFile written, then straight through lk/linkEntry! and llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative!, as compilePackageToLlvm! does past its checker call.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#buildNative" :text "The path of name's native executable, compiled from src and linked against libaslrt.a.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#childCpuUs" :text "User plus system CPU microseconds of every child this process has waited for, -1 when getrusage fails.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#rawCaller" :text "m.caller: the boxed constant %a passed to opBuiltin rawId in the entry block and again in both branch blocks, so a rewrite of rawId into a call of m.raw (i64 -> i64) must unbox the argument and rebox the result in three blocks of one function.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#testRewriteRawSignature" :text "rewriteModuleBuiltins on a hand-built module whose resolved callee takes and returns raw i64: the result verifies (each argument unboxed to the param type, each result reboxed, every fresh temp defined once per function across its blocks), and the counts of unbox, box and call instructions are exactly one per rewritten opBuiltin.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#testRequestedBuiltin" :text "A prelude-defined builtin name the prelude itself reaches by an ordinary call (isFinite? calls floatInf as prelude.floatInf, so floatInf is already requested before the opBuiltin rewrite looks) is still rewritten where the program calls it as opBuiltin, and the native result equals asl-host run.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#testLateBuiltin" :text "An opBuiltin that first appears in a definition lowered after the overlay step (here a prelude whose floatInf body calls bytesSha256, reached only through the program's opBuiltin floatInf) is still rewritten to the overlay's native.bytesSha256: the overlay and prelude rewrite rounds repeat until neither seeds a new name.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#testCollidingDefinitionName" :text "link.asl finding 1 (grade PRELUDEASL-0): the native overlay's sha256.asl defines and internally calls its own mask32; a prelude that also happens to define a function named mask32, called from another prelude function, must not have either definition silently dropped by a shared unqualified requested list. A program calling bytesSha256 (seeding native's own internal mask32 need) and the custom prelude's triggerMask32 (seeding prelude's distinct mask32 need) must end up with both native.mask32 and prelude.mask32 lowered; pre-fix, whichever unit's bare 'mask32' request lands in LinkAcc.requested first starves the other, so its definition never reaches acc.modules even though verifySsa does not catch the missing callee (that only surfaces as an undefined symbol at the C/LLVM link step).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/nativeOverlayTest.asl#testOverlayErrors" :text "A broken or unreadable overlay file is a link error, not a silent fall back to the C builtin it shadows; a missing overlay directory is an empty overlay; and linkUnitsWith reports the overlay error instead of linking without it.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/stringRepeatTest.asl#" :text "Correctness and scaling tests for prelude stringRepeat")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#" :text "Pure ASL decoder parity over every checked Zstandard fixture plus native overlay parity")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeJoinRun" :text "One join pass: each run of sixteen adjacent parts and their fifteen separators becomes one balanced tree of stringConcat calls (no Pair, Option or closure per element; a shorter last run goes to preludeJoinShort), so the list shrinks sixteenfold per pass; self tail calls keep the stack O(1) and the result list comes back reversed. A bytes buffer filled in one pass would be linear, but no floor primitive turns Bytes into a String, and variadic str costs about 56ns per argument natively.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/prelude.asl#preludeJoinAll" :text "Repeats preludeJoinRun with the same separator until one string remains: log16 n passes of about two stringConcat calls per part, replacing the pairwise fold (log2 n passes, a Pair and an Option per element per pass); stringJoinTest measures it at a quarter of the pairwise time on asl-host and a third natively.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#overlayProgram" :text "A program that decodes every fixture with zstdDecompress and prints, per fixture, the decoded length and Adler-32 (computed in ASL, so the native run never reaches a C digest builtin or the slow bytesSha256 overlay) or the exact error text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#nativeFixtureParity!" :text "The fixture program is linked by lk/linkEntry! (which applies the asl/prelude/native overlay rewrite), emitted by llvm/emitLlvmProgramNative! with the host routes, as compilePackageToLlvm! emits, and linked by clang against libaslrt.a, as nativeOverlayTest does for bytesSha256; the emitted IR must define native.zstdDecompress and name no zstdDecompress runtime builtin, and the binary's output over every positive, parquet-page and negative fixture must equal asl-host run (the C decoder) byte for byte. Every step runs and the mktemp work directory is removed before the first assertion, so a failing assertion leaves nothing behind.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#mask32" :text "32-bit word arithmetic kept inside int64 by explicit masking: shrWord and shlWord are single >> and << instructions natively; every operand is under 2^32 and every shift this file uses is under 32, so (<< x n) stays under 2^63, and addWord's sum of at most five terms each under 2^32 stays under 2^35, so none of the shifts, + or * below can overflow int64 and trap")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#roundK" :text "the 64 round constants (FIPS 180-4 4.2.2), indexed by a cond chain rather than an array: the overlay has no array builtin to call, only the Bytes it already needs for the message schedule")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#paddedLen" :text "the padded buffer: next multiple of 64 that leaves room for 0x80 and the 8-byte length no matter n mod 64, as asl/host/src/prelude.c bSha256's own tl computation does")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#loadSchedule" :text "the message schedule for one block, 256 bytes holding 64 32-bit words, w[0..15] copied from the block and w[16..63] built by smallSigma0/smallSigma1")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/native/sha256.asl#round" :text "one round per call over the eight working variables as Int64 parameters, so the 64 rounds of a block build no record and read no field; only the block's result is a ShaState")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#windowFrame" :text "1 KiB window, two raw 600-byte blocks, then one RLE-mode sequence (ll 0, ml 3) whose offset off stays within the 1200 bytes already produced; the backward bitstream is the 1-sequence offset value off+3 whose top bit is the padding marker")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#repeatOffsetIdx2Frame" :text "default reps (1,4,8); block1 is 10 raw bytes [1..10], block2 has two sequences each (ll 1, ofv 3): both land on idx 2, which per RFC 8878 reads rep[2] then sets rep[1]=old rep[0], rep[2]=old rep[1]. Sequence 1 reads rep[2]=8 (copying block1[3..5]=[4,5,6] after literal 'A') and updates rep to (8,1,4). Sequence 2 reads the NEW rep[2]=4 (copying output[11..13]=[4,5,6] after literal 'B'), which a mutant that leaves rep[2] stale (treating idx 2 like idx 1, not updating it) would instead read as the old rep[2]=8 (copying block1[7..9]=[8,9,10]): the two decoders then disagree on bytes 15..17")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#offsetJustPastProducedFrame" :text "1 KiB window (windowLog 10), one raw 10-byte block, then one full-offset sequence (ll 0, ml 3, ofv 14 so off = ofv-3 = 11) that reaches exactly one byte past the 10 bytes already produced: window (1024) comfortably covers offset 11, so only the produced-bound guard (off > baseOut+produced+ll) can reject it; a mutant that relaxes that guard by one lets this exact offset through into an out-of-range match copy")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/zstdAslTest.asl#checkedFrameSha" :text "frames from zstd 1.5.7 --check -19 over the first n bytes of MANIFESTO.md; lengths 5, 13, 45, 77 and 100 leave a remainder past the 32-byte stripes, so the xxh64 8-byte and 4-byte tail rounds run, which the 0, 1 and 32-multiple file fixtures skip")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/preludeListAllocTest.asl#main" :text "ELAUDIT-C3: listAll? listAny? listTake listDrop walked their list via optionOr(listTail xs)(list), which wastes an object per element beyond the host's unavoidable Option-wrapper cost; rewritten to match on (listTail xs) directly (as preludeDropSpan already did). This file runs itself as a subprocess (asl-host run ... SCENARIO), through tools/fleet/run so the child is timeout- and descendant-bounded and killed on a verdict (rule spawnSafety); the parent process is never the running executable.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/preludeListAllocTest.asl#allOnlyFirst" :text "preludeHead on an empty list traps (non-exhaustive match on none, per the doc at listHead/listTail's unwrap helpers); used here only as a probe that must never run, to prove listAll?/listAny? stop at the first decisive element instead of forcing the whole list")
(:doc :symbol "asl/prelude/tests/preludeListAllocTest.asl#runScenario" :text "spawns the one-shot measuring subprocess through tools/fleet/run (rule spawnSafety): a timeout and descendant limit bound it, and a verdict kills its whole tree; this file never starts asl-host directly via a bare shell/processRun call")
